    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "There are plans to build about 100 new data centres in the UK. These centres will "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " many new jobs. But not everyone is happy. Some people are "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " that these centres could also damage the environment."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Data centres are large buildings that hold powerful computers. These computers "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "process",
            "ref": "v-process"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " our digital information. They make the internet work. They save our emails and photos. We need more data centres because the "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "computing power",
            "ref": "v-computing-power"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is rising fast. For example, artificial intelligence (AI) requires powerful computers to learn and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "generate",
            "ref": "v-generate"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " content."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Last year, the UK Government said data centres are the key to the country’s "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "infrastructure",
            "ref": "v-infrastructure"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They are as "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " as power stations or hospitals. Data centres are the engines of modern life. They keep our personal information safe. If a storm or power "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "cut",
            "ref": "v-cut"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " occurs, the Government will make sure these centres keep "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "However, there are problems. These centres use a huge amount of electricity. They also get very hot, so they need a lot of water to stay "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Most of the new centres will be built near London. But this area is already “water-stressed”. This means it often runs low on water. Scientists warn that new data centres could make this problem "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Data centres use a lot of power. By 2026, the world’s data centres might use as much electricity as the whole country of Japan uses now. If there is not enough clean electricity, power companies might have to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " fossil fuels. This creates "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". However, some big companies are trying to help. They want to use clean energy, like wind power, to run their computers."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
